files.change:
Append a single trailing newline. The file currently ends `COMMIT;` with no `\n` (`tail -c 1 ... | xxd` returns `00000000: 3b`). It becomes three newline-terminated lines:

BEGIN TRANSACTION;
ALTER TABLE transactions ADD COLUMN schedule_occurrence INTEGER DEFAULT NULL;
COMMIT;

Do not change anything else in the file. Migrations are keyed by filename rather than content, so databases that already ran it are unaffected. Note this is a majority convention, not a universal one: 49 of the 55 .sql files in this directory end in 0x0a and five pre-existing ones do not (see out_of_scope).
